# Code comments (required)

When writing or editing code in this project, **always add comments**. The user explicitly wants this — do not skip comments for brevity.

## What to comment

- **Class / file**: short docblock describing purpose and how it fits the feature
- **Public methods**: what they do, important inputs/outputs, API side effects
- **Non-obvious logic**: why (not what) — e.g. 12h↔24h time, settings vs DB tables, AR|EN field pairs, offline-only courses
- **Sections** in large files: brief `//` markers (hero, sponsor, events, …)
- **Migrations / seeders**: what the change is for

## Style

- Prefer PHPDoc on classes and methods; use `//` for inline “why”
- Keep comments accurate and concise — explain intent, constraints, and gotchas
- Update comments when behavior changes; remove comments that become wrong
- Do not comment obvious one-liners (`$i++`, simple getters) unless the surrounding context is unclear

## Reminder

If you ship new Filament forms, API services, models, or routes without comments, that is incomplete work for this repo.
